Scidc - Chess Database
======================

Scidc is a chess database application, forked from Scidb r1531.
It supports reading and writing multiple database formats and includes
built-in chess engine support for game analysis. No engines are bundled;
they can be fetched from their original projects from within the
application.

Most changes in this fork were developed with the assistance of
Claude (Anthropic AI) and Mistral (Mistral AI).

Supported formats
-----------------
- SI5 / SI4 / SI3  (Scid formats, read/write)
- SCI / SCV        (Scidb formats, read/write)
- CBH / CBF        (ChessBase, read only)
- PGN              (import/export)

Requirements
------------
- Linux (x86_64)
- For running: none (AppImage bundles all dependencies)
- For building: gcc/g++, make, Tcl/Tk 9.0 dev headers (including the
  private ones), X11 dev headers
  (expat and zlib are built from src/util/ and linked statically)

Installation
------------
Scidc is distributed as an AppImage. No installation is required.

Download Scidc-x86_64.AppImage, make it executable and run it:

    chmod +x Scidc-x86_64.AppImage
    ./Scidc-x86_64.AppImage

User data is stored in ~/.scidc-beta/

Building from source
--------------------
See the file INSTALL for detailed build instructions.

Maintainer scripts
------------------
- bump-version.sh    raise the build counter in all version files and rebuild
- build-appimage.sh  build the AppImage
- release.sh         publish a built AppImage as a release: tag, upload, and
                     verify by downloading the asset back and running it

See the file INSTALL for details.

